# dbt conventions

Project: `supply_chain_dbt`. Raw tables live in source `raw` (`models/staging/sources.yml`).

## Naming

Prefix every model by layer. One model per file; the file name matches the model name.

| Prefix | Layer | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `stg_` | Staging: rename, cast, light cleanup of one source | `stg_purchase_orders` |
| `int_` | Intermediate: joins and business logic | `int_shipment_delays` |
| `fct_` | Fact: events or metrics at a grain | `fct_shipments` |
| `dim_` | Dimension: descriptive entities | `dim_suppliers` |

Put staging models under `models/staging/`, intermediate under `models/intermediate/`, and facts and dimensions under `models/marts/`.

## Dependencies

Reference other models with `{{ ref('model_name') }}` and raw tables with `{{ source('raw', 'table_name') }}`. Never hardcode a database, schema, or table name in `FROM` / `JOIN`.

```sql
-- good
from {{ source('raw', 'shipments') }} sh
join {{ ref('stg_purchase_orders') }} po using (po_id)

-- bad
from raw.shipments sh
join main.stg_purchase_orders po using (po_id)
```

## Tests

Every new or changed model gets a `schema.yml` entry in the same folder:

- A one-line `description`
- `not_null` and `unique` (or a compound unique test) on the grain / primary key
- `relationships` tests when a column is a foreign key to another model

```yaml
models:
  - name: stg_purchase_orders
    description: Cleaned purchase orders from raw.
    columns:
      - name: po_id
        data_tests:
          - unique
          - not_null
```
